   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "scm_step1410_physics_column",
     "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, p_top = 177.6 hPa, data/eqwefic/scm_ref) dumped by the instrumented ctessum-claude/WRF fork (module_esm_dump, commit 592f693) at TWO levels for the same step: the PHYSICS-DRIVER level (hooks around radiation_driver, surface_driver + pbl_driver and the physics-tendency sum in dyn_em/module_first_rk_step_part1.F -- dumps subassembly_all, _pbl and _rad) and the KERNEL level (sfclayrev, sw, ysu and rrtm scm_ref dumps of the same call). The seven dumps are merged into one column namespace by tools/merge_dumps.py (esm_dump_scm_suite_<step>.json, variables tagged all_/pbl_/rad_/sfc_/sw_/ysu_/rrtm_) because tools/fill_tests.py admits two dumps per test; the numbers are transcribed by fill_tests.py from the sidecar couplings/scm_physics_column.esm.fill.json. All references are real32 model values. The DRIVER-level tendency vector (rthblten, rublten, rvblten, rqvblten, rqcblten, rqiblten, rthraten, rth_phys_sum, hfx, qfx, gsw, glw, olr, pblh) is the contract this document exists to pin: it is what WRF hands to the dynamics, and rqcblten/rqiblten are asserted here for the first time. Regime: WRF step 1410 (kernel call 2820), 18:29 UTC = 12:02 local solar time -- the strongest daytime forcing of the 24 h reference run: gsw = 549.7 W/m^2 (cos zenith 0.639), glw = 268.9, olr = 256.0, slab hfx = 173.6 W/m^2 (SfclayRev's own 173.5), Ri_b = -0.118 (regime 4, free convection), u* = 0.454 m/s, h = 926 m over 16 layers, tsk = 288.5 K, and only a trace of cirrus aloft (qi <= 2.1e-9, three cloudy layers), so YSU's cloud-top entrainment branch is inactive and no liquid cloud is present. Residuals of the whole assembly against the step-1410 references, measured with zero tolerances: surface-layer outputs <= 1.9e-6 relative (rmol; hfx 5.4e-7, u* 4.0e-8, qsfc / z0 / regime exact), PBL height 6.4e-7 relative and kpbl exact, K_h / K_m Linf 2.3e-4 / 1.6e-4 m^2/s, longwave fluxes Linf 2.3e-4 (F_up) and 1.3e-4 W/m^2 (F_dn), dthdt_lw and rthraten 5.2e-9 K/s, dthdt_sw 1.6e-10 K/s, gsw 1.4e-6, glw 2.4e-7 and olr 3.2e-7 relative, and the PBL tendencies 1.1e-4 K/s (rthblten, column max 3.7e-4), 6.1e-5 and 3.0e-5 m/s^2 (rublten / rvblten, max 2.8e-4 / 3.2e-4), 1.4e-8 1/s (rqvblten, max 3.3e-7), rqcblten exactly zero (no cloud water) and rqiblten 1.5e-18 (max 1.3e-16). The PBL TENDENCIES are asserted only LOOSELY and document a known gap rather than test the physics: WRF's rthblten/rublten/rvblten/rqvblten/rqcblten/rqiblten are the IMPLICIT tridiagonal step's (c_new - c_old)/dt at dt = 60 s while the assembly evaluates the instantaneous right-hand side (PLAN.md 0.3), which at this regime is the dominant term of their residual; the physics itself is pinned by ysu.esm's own small-dt tests, and a stage-3 comparison at the WRF step must apply the same implicit step to the assembled tendencies. The driver-level th2/t2/q2 are overwritten by the land-surface branch of surface_driver, so those three are referenced to the kernel-level sfclayrev dump, and the slab's driver-level hfx/qfx are prescribed (hfx_lsm/qfx_lsm) because the land scheme is not co-mounted -- see the model description. TOLERANCES: each is the smallest of {1, 2, 5} x 10^k that is at least 5x the residual measured in a zero-tolerance run (relative for the scalars, absolute for the Linf_error column assertions), with a 1e-6 relative floor; an assertion that is exact at zero tolerance keeps abs 0. ",
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "psfc0": 97142.90625,
      "tsk0": 288.5369873046875,
      "xland0": 1.0,
      "mavail0": 0.6000000238418579,
      "pblh_prev0": 924.8997802734375,
      "u10": 3.9584646224975586,
      "v10": -4.2198567390441895,
      "t10": 284.63226318359375,
      "qv10": 0.0047745187766849995,
      "p10": 96843.859375,
      "dz10": 51.57603454589844,
      "dx0": 4000.0,
      "lakemask0": 0.0,
      "water_depth0": 0.0,
      "znt_prev0": 0.05000000074505806,
      "ust_prev0": 0.4540386199951172,
      "mol_prev0": -0.319833904504776,
      "qsfc_prev0": 0.011381950229406357,
      "hfx_prev0": 173.76504516601562,
      "qfx_prev0": 8.09187040431425e-05,
      "ustm_prev0": 0.4356035590171814,
      "chs_prev0": 0.0,
      "chs2_prev0": 0.0,
      "cqs2_prev0": 138.677978515625,
      "isfflx0": 1.0,
      "shalwater_z00": 0.0,
      "scm_force_flux0": 0.0,
      "isftcflx0": 0.0,
      "iz0tlnd0": 0.0,
      "topdown0": 1.0,
      "hfx_lsm0": 173.59681701660156,
      "qfx_lsm0": 8.102758874883875e-05,
      "co2vmr0": 0.00037900000461377203,
      "n2ovmr0": 3.1900000863060995e-07,
      "ch4vmr0": 1.7739999975674436e-06,
      "emiss0": 0.9200000166893005,
      "csza0": 0.6393358707427979,
      "albedo0": 0.20000000298023224,
      "solcon0": 1385.0826416015625,
      "obscur0": 0.0,
      "cssca0": 9.999999747378752e-06,
      "icloud0": 1.0
     },
     "time_span": {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 1
     },
     "assertions": [
      {
       "variable": "sfc_hfx",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": 173.466064453125,
